{
  "id": "29104_fukusu",
  "headword": "{服|ふく}す",
  "reading": "ふくす",
  "romaji": "fukusu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to comply with; to observe; to submit to",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to observe; to comply with; to submit to (a rule, period, or authority)",
      "explanation": "To follow or observe a prescribed duty, rule, or period. Most commonly used in the phrase 喪に服す (to observe mourning). Also written 服する, the longer form."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29104_fukusu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{喪|も}に{服|ふく}す。",
      "english": "To observe mourning.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29104_fukusu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{親|おや}の{死後|しご}、{一年間|いちねんかん}{喪|も}に{服|ふく}した。",
      "english": "After my parent's death, I observed mourning for one year.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29104_fukusu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{判決|はんけつ}に{服|ふく}して{刑務所|けいむしょ}に{入|はい}った。",
      "english": "He submitted to the verdict and entered prison.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal verb most commonly encountered in the fixed phrase {喪|も}に{服|ふく}す (to be in mourning). The longer form {服|ふく}する is equally correct and more common in writing.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {喪|も}に{服|ふく}す: to observe mourning\n- {判決|はんけつ}に{服|ふく}す: to submit to a court ruling\n- {命令|めいれい}に{服|ふく}す: to comply with an order\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {従|したが}う: to follow, to obey — more general, everyday usage\n- {従事|じゅうじ}する: to engage in, to be involved in — used for occupations",
